═══ CODE RULES ═══
- Always TypeScript. Never .js in src/.
- All props, state, args, return types must be explicitly typed.
- Never use 'any'. Use 'unknown' + type guards.
- All shared types in src/types/scan.ts.
- interface for object shapes. type for unions/primitives.
- Functional components ONLY. Never class components.
- NEVER dangerouslySetInnerHTML — ever. XSS protection is critical.
- Destructure props at function signature level.
- Every useEffect needs complete dependency array + cleanup.
- Never call navigate() inside render — only in handlers or useEffect.
- NEVER throw unhandled errors to UI. Every error has user-facing fallback.
- NEVER show raw errors, stack traces, or HTTP codes to users.
- Edge Function errors return HTTP 200 with { error: true } — never 500.
- Navigate to /error on unrecoverable frontend failure.

Naming: Components=PascalCase | functions=camelCase | interfaces=IPascalCase | types=PascalCase | handlers=handleX | booleans=isX/hasX | constants=SCREAMING_SNAKE

