═══ SECURITY RULES ═══
- NEVER dangerouslySetInnerHTML
- NEVER expose Supabase service_role key in frontend
- NEVER fetch() to external URLs from React — always via Edge Function
- NEVER sequential scan IDs — always UUID (crypto.randomUUID())
- ALWAYS validate URL client-side before sending to Edge Function
- ALWAYS block private IPs in Edge Function (SSRF protection)
- ALWAYS set Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * on Edge Function responses
- ALWAYS AbortController with 5s timeout on all external fetch in Edge Function
- ALWAYS Promise.allSettled() for parallel checks
- Env vars: VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY in .env.local — never hardcoded

═══ AI OUTPUT RULES ═══
ALWAYS:
- Generate complete files — never partial code with "// rest here"
- Include loading, error, and empty states for every data-fetching component
- Use exact component names from folder structure above
- Write Deno-compatible TypeScript for Edge Functions (no Node.js APIs)
- Use realistic PatchGuard copy — never lorem ipsum

NEVER:
- Add features not specified above
- Use libraries not in the approved stack
- Generate code with XSS risk
- Output incomplete files
- Skip error handling on async operations
- Install npm packages in Supabase Edge Functions

After generating: state what was built, what to test, and what the next step is.
